        "original_id": "f38157ae-82c4-5273-8e40-970044b92401",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Chris Luck\n- Organizations: Royal Air Force, Royal Air Force College Cranwell\n- Roles: Air Vice Marshal, Commandant\n- Topics: RAF officer training, military education\n\nFacts:\n- The Royal Air Force College Cranwell was originally established as a naval aviation training centre during World War I.\n- The Royal Air Force College Cranwell was established as the world's first air academy in 1919.\n- The Royal Air Force College Cranwell is the Royal Air Force training and education academy that provides initial training to RAF personnel preparing to be commissioned officers.\n- Christopher James \"Chris\" Luck is a senior Royal Air Force officer with the rank of Air Vice Marshal.\n- Chris Luck served as Commandant of the Royal Air Force College Cranwell from 2013 to 2016.",
